Chuck was the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequin]] servant assigned to the Party's berth aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. He wore the pinstriped clothes of his order under a cape and carried a scepter, and he answered to any name, having told the Party to call him Butler or Thing; they settled on Chuck. He appeared as a big brown cat.

He walked his guests through growing a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] from a [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone]], was quick to bow and vanish in a puff of smoke, and gave the Party a small figurine of himself that summons him when it is crushed. He carried them about the strider on a floating disc of black stone and said he could not teach the spell, since he is a sorcerer and the magic is inborn. He acknowledged the gods but did not worship as the Party does. He said he was of little use away from the strider, and offered to have their car lowered off it whenever they wish to leave. He was quick-tongued and less servile than he once was, complaining of being summoned so often and saying he never signed up for the work. Asked for a map he first claimed to have none, then led the Party by a safe, quick route to the town's library and its curator, [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Ocelith|Ocelith]], and gave [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] another figurine of himself.

Chuck is dead. When the Party crushed his figurine, it appeared as a desiccated corpse in Harlequin attire that collapsed where it stood.
